1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,980
This rocket is about to go to space.

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:04,020
And we're going with it, all the way.

3
00:00:04,540 --> 00:00:06,700
But before the countdown hits zero, let's

4
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:07,520
look inside.

5
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,100
Almost all of it is fuel.

6
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:10,780
About ninety percent.

7
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,560
The engines, the tanks, the capsule and

8
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,916
the crew all fit in the last ten percent.

9
00:00:17,416 --> 00:00:18,216
See that water?

10
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:19,896
A flood of it pours onto the pad.

11
00:00:20,376 --> 00:00:22,876
A rocket is so loud, its own noise could

12
00:00:22,896 --> 00:00:23,856
shake the pad apart.

13
00:00:24,496 --> 00:00:25,876
The water soaks up that noise.

14
00:00:28,316 --> 00:00:29,076
Ignition.

15
00:00:29,096 --> 00:00:29,896
Notice something?

16
00:00:30,416 --> 00:00:32,336
The engines are roaring, but the rocket

17
00:00:32,356 --> 00:00:33,156
hasn't moved.

18
00:00:33,676 --> 00:00:35,456
That's because the push from the engines

19
00:00:35,476 --> 00:00:37,356
has to grow bigger than the rocket's weight.

20
00:00:37,956 --> 00:00:39,836
About five hundred tonnes.

21
00:00:39,856 --> 00:00:41,736
Only when the push wins, does it rise.

22
00:00:42,156 --> 00:00:43,036
And there it goes.

23
00:00:43,656 --> 00:00:45,136
It isn't pushing against the ground.

24
00:00:45,596 --> 00:00:48,136
It throws hot gas downwards, really fast,

25
00:00:48,376 --> 00:00:50,116
and that gas pushes the rocket up.

26
00:00:50,656 --> 00:00:52,536
Exactly like a balloon when you let it go.

27
00:00:53,096 --> 00:00:53,896
Now watch.

28
00:00:54,276 --> 00:00:55,336
It starts to lean over.

29
00:00:55,776 --> 00:00:56,576
That's on purpose.

30
00:00:57,016 --> 00:00:58,696
Getting high is the easy part.

31
00:00:59,176 --> 00:01:01,316
To stay in space, you need to go sideways,

32
00:01:01,636 --> 00:01:02,436
incredibly fast.

33
00:01:02,976 --> 00:01:05,156
So the rocket slowly turns its climb into

34
00:01:05,176 --> 00:01:06,136
a sideways sprint.

35
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:09,093
About a minute in, the air pushes against

36
00:01:09,113 --> 00:01:10,113
the rocket the hardest.

37
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,733
So the engines ease back for a few seconds,

38
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:14,833
the rocket slips through, and then it's

39
00:01:14,853 --> 00:01:15,793
full power again.

40
00:01:16,483 --> 00:01:18,223
Inside, the crew are pressed into their

41
00:01:18,243 --> 00:01:20,823
seats, around three times heavier than normal.

42
00:01:21,363 --> 00:01:23,323
Two and a half minutes in, the first stage

43
00:01:23,343 --> 00:01:24,323
is nearly empty.

44
00:01:24,903 --> 00:01:26,743
An empty tank is just dead weight.

45
00:01:27,303 --> 00:01:29,483
Every kilo you carry needs more fuel to

46
00:01:29,503 --> 00:01:30,083
lift.

47
00:01:30,103 --> 00:01:31,703
So the rocket simply lets it go.

48
00:01:32,423 --> 00:01:33,223
Separation.

49
00:01:33,443 --> 00:01:35,403
The second engine lights, and the nose cone

50
00:01:35,423 --> 00:01:36,223
opens.

51
00:01:36,403 --> 00:01:37,283
And that first stage?

52
00:01:37,783 --> 00:01:39,763
Some rockets fly it back, flip it over,

53
00:01:39,963 --> 00:01:41,763
and land it on a ship in the ocean, so it

54
00:01:41,783 --> 00:01:42,583
can fly again.

55
00:01:43,183 --> 00:01:44,943
That's why spaceflight is getting cheaper.

56
00:01:45,503 --> 00:01:47,043
A few minutes later, we're in orbit.

57
00:01:47,543 --> 00:01:48,503
Here's the big secret.

58
00:01:49,343 --> 00:01:50,143
Orbit isn't floating.

59
00:01:50,363 --> 00:01:51,163
It's falling.

60
00:01:51,383 --> 00:01:53,883
Fire a ball sideways from a very tall mountain,

61
00:01:54,103 --> 00:01:54,903
and it falls.

62
00:01:55,263 --> 00:01:56,723
Faster, and it lands farther.

63
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:59,443
Fast enough, and the Earth curves away as

64
00:01:59,463 --> 00:02:00,303
fast as it falls.

65
00:02:00,723 --> 00:02:02,683
It keeps falling, and keeps missing.

66
00:02:03,383 --> 00:02:05,103
That takes about twenty eight thousand kilometres

67
00:02:05,123 --> 00:02:05,923
an hour.

68
00:02:06,303 --> 00:02:07,943
Fast enough to go all the way around the

69
00:02:07,963 --> 00:02:09,383
Earth in about ninety minutes.

70
00:02:09,923 --> 00:02:12,023
So the crew see around sixteen sunrises,

71
00:02:12,043 --> 00:02:13,303
every single day.

72
00:02:13,703 --> 00:02:15,743
And they float, not because gravity is gone,

73
00:02:15,963 --> 00:02:17,583
but because they are falling too, together

74
00:02:17,603 --> 00:02:18,523
with their spacecraft.

75
00:02:19,223 --> 00:02:21,383
When the mission is done, coming home starts

76
00:02:21,403 --> 00:02:22,423
with slowing down.

77
00:02:22,963 --> 00:02:24,983
The capsule turns around, and drops back

78
00:02:25,003 --> 00:02:25,803
into the air.

79
00:02:26,003 --> 00:02:27,243
That glow isn't friction.

80
00:02:27,623 --> 00:02:30,163
The capsule is so fast that the air in front

81
00:02:30,183 --> 00:02:32,963
gets squeezed, and squeezed air gets incredibly

82
00:02:32,983 --> 00:02:33,783
hot.

83
00:02:34,043 --> 00:02:35,103
Around fifteen hundred degrees.

84
00:02:35,663 --> 00:02:37,403
The heat shield takes it, burning away,

85
00:02:37,423 --> 00:02:38,863
layer by layer, on purpose.

86
00:02:39,523 --> 00:02:40,323
Then it gets quiet.

87
00:02:40,983 --> 00:02:42,823
Small parachutes first, then the big ones.

88
00:02:43,383 --> 00:02:44,183
Slower, and slower.

89
00:02:44,663 --> 00:02:45,383
Splash.

90
00:02:45,403 --> 00:02:46,203
Welcome home.

91
00:02:46,503 --> 00:02:48,383
From a countdown, to the sky, to space,

92
00:02:48,403 --> 00:02:49,623
and back, in one trip.

93
00:02:49,963 --> 00:02:52,403
Mostly fuel, one tiny capsule, and a whole

94
00:02:52,423 --> 00:02:53,223
lot of falling.

95
00:02:53,623 --> 00:02:55,543
And yes, the first thing the astronaut asks

96
00:02:55,563 --> 00:02:56,443
for, is chai.

97
00:02:58,243 --> 00:02:59,043
Mission complete.

98
00:02:59,623 --> 00:03:00,663
Thanks for flying with us.
